  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The overview of the built environment is presented as a series of individual essays, which may result in a fragmented rather than a fully unified historical narrative.",
      "what": "This collection of historical essays synthesizes research on the built environment of British cities between 1945 and 2000. It brings together diverse sub-disciplinary perspectives to document the physical and architectural evolution of urban spaces across the United Kingdom during the post-war era.",
      "why": "It provides a multi-faceted historical record of late-twentieth-century British urbanism, offering a consolidated reference for how post-war planning and architectural shifts physically reshaped the nation's cities."
    }
